WEBVTT

00:00:00.015 --> 00:00:03.329
Easy Greek Myths. Icarus and His Wings.

00:00:03.329 --> 00:00:06.790
Daedalus was the cleverest builder in all of Greece.

00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:09.953
He built wonderful things for the king of an island.

00:00:09.953 --> 00:00:14.094
But the king did not want him to leave and share his secrets.

00:00:14.094 --> 00:00:18.392
So he kept Daedalus and his young son Icarus on the island.

00:00:18.392 --> 00:00:22.390
Ships could not take them, because the king watched the sea.

00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:26.028
"The king rules the land and the sea," said Daedalus.

00:00:26.028 --> 00:00:28.088
"But he does not rule the air."

00:00:28.088 --> 00:00:30.931
He began to collect feathers from birds.

00:00:30.931 --> 00:00:34.072
He tied them together and fixed them with wax.

00:00:34.072 --> 00:00:39.757
In the end he had made two pairs of wings, one for himself and one for his son.

00:00:39.757 --> 00:00:42.528
"Listen carefully," he told Icarus.

00:00:42.528 --> 00:00:47.315
"Do not fly too low, or the sea will make your wings wet and heavy.

00:00:47.315 --> 00:00:51.576
And do not fly too high, or the sun will melt the wax.

00:00:51.576 --> 00:00:52.975
Stay close to me."

00:00:52.975 --> 00:00:56.157
They jumped into the air and flew out over the sea.

00:00:56.157 --> 00:00:58.837
The island became small behind them.

00:00:58.837 --> 00:00:59.988
They were free.

00:00:59.988 --> 00:01:02.622
Icarus had never felt so happy.

00:01:02.622 --> 00:01:04.244
He flew in circles.

00:01:04.244 --> 00:01:05.986
He flew up and down.

00:01:05.986 --> 00:01:07.770
Flying was so easy!

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:10.292
He forgot what his father had said.

00:01:10.292 --> 00:01:13.411
He flew higher and higher, up toward the sun.

00:01:13.411 --> 00:01:15.602
The sun was hot on his back.

00:01:15.602 --> 00:01:17.484
The wax became soft.

00:01:17.484 --> 00:01:20.593
One by one, the feathers began to fall.

00:01:20.593 --> 00:01:24.313
Icarus moved his arms, but there were no wings left.

00:01:24.313 --> 00:01:26.278
He fell down into the sea.

00:01:26.278 --> 00:01:27.965
Daedalus looked around.

00:01:27.965 --> 00:01:31.071
"Icarus, where are you?" he shouted.

00:01:31.071 --> 00:01:34.634
Then he saw the feathers on the water, and he knew.

00:01:34.634 --> 00:01:37.867
He flew on alone, and he never flew again.
